# Regression for gorget-js snag #2: a concrete-vs-concrete call-arg
# type mismatch in code reached through an `Item::Module` wrapper
# (i.e. an imported file) must surface as a hard error, not be silently
# swallowed by the imported-module error-truncate in
# `check_items_recursive_tc`.
#
# The mismatch lives in `impl.gg` (`unwrap_tagged(float_arg)`), which is
# imported and therefore processed under the truncate path. Before the
# fix, the call silently compiled and the function returned junk
# (the float's bit pattern reinterpreted as an enum tag). After the fix,
# the hard-error path in `Expr::Call`'s arg unify pushes a TypeMismatch
# into `hard_errors`, which the truncate re-appends.

from impl import silent_call_bug

void main():
    int x = silent_call_bug()
    print(f"{x}")
